+## Revision-Based Concurrency
 
-## Submission and Retrieval
+Each visit submission names its base revision ID. A submission creating a new visit uses `null` as its base. A submission editing an existing visit names the revision ID it started from. When a submission's base matches the current revision, it becomes the new current revision. When a submission's base does not match current (a concurrent edit occurred), both the existing current revision and the new submission remain as competing revisions requiring coordinator resolution.
 
